1
00:01:20,628 --> 00:01:26,074
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراً

2
00:01:30,175 --> 00:01:39,226
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه, as we mentioned, would constantly meet,

3
00:01:41,042 --> 00:01:47,777
with the people to get feedback on their leaders.

4
00:01:49,689 --> 00:01:53,635
He wanted to know how the Wulaa(ولآه) were doing.

5
00:01:54,897 --> 00:02:06,123
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه would meet with the people to get feedback, on the Umara'a(أمرآء),

6
00:02:09,203 --> 00:02:15,819
and he would take their concerns seriously, and he would act upon it.

7
00:02:16,945 --> 00:02:23,641
And I'll give examples of some of the complaints that were raised against some of the wulaa(ولآه)

8
00:02:28,306 --> 00:02:30,481
Some men from Bannu Asad(بنوأسد) from Kufa(كوفه).

9
00:02:32,423 --> 00:02:35,192
They came to Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه,

10
00:02:37,735 --> 00:02:40,372
and they complained about Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن أبي وقاص).

11
00:02:42,685 --> 00:02:46,864
Saad Bin Abi Waqas رضي الله عنه, is  one of the 10 given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

12
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:53,941
One of the first believers and they came and complained about him,

13
00:02:55,531 --> 00:02:58,276
and they chose an interesting timing.

14
00:03:01,281 --> 00:03:08,586
It happened while the Muslims and the Persians were preparing for war.

15
00:03:10,174 --> 00:03:16,279
The Muslims were preparing and the Persians were preparing for the great battle of Nahwand(النہوند).

16
00:03:19,404 --> 00:03:24,973
So, these men knew very well that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) especially before a battle would start,

17
00:03:25,901 --> 00:03:29,346
 he wanted to make sure of Wahdat-As-Saff(الوحدت الصف), the unity of the Muslims,

18
00:03:30,504 --> 00:03:34,884
 because the last thing you don't want to do, is go to battle when you have the disunity.

19
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:40,466
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) as very, very keen on ensuring,

20
00:03:40,942 --> 00:03:44,656
that the Muslims Jama'at(جماعة) is unified and one.

21
00:03:45,287 --> 00:03:50,519
There's no dissent, there's no division, there's no Fitnah(فِتْنَه), there's no gossip.

22
00:03:52,351 --> 00:03:55,199
He wanted to make sure that the Muslims are on one heart.

23
00:03:57,515 --> 00:04:06,744
So, for them to choose that timing right before the Battle of Nahwand(نهوند) tells you something.

24
00:04:10,114 --> 00:04:12,784
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),when he heard their complaints. He said;

25
00:04:14,293 --> 00:04:22,827
إِنَّا لدَّلِيْلَ عَلَى مَا عِنْدَ كُمْ مِنَّ الشَّرْ،نَحُوْضَاكُمْ فِيْ هَذَالْاَمْرِ، وَإِنِ سّتَعَدَّلَكُمْ مَنِ سّتَعَدُّوْ وَإَيْمُالله

26
00:04:23,398 --> 00:04:27,425
لَا يَمْنَعَنِيْ ذَالِكَ مِنَ النَّظَرِ فِيْ مَا لَدَيْكُمْ وَإِنْ نَظَرُبِكُمْ

27
00:04:28,655 --> 00:04:36,717
It is evident that you have evil intentions in your complaints

28
00:04:37,624 --> 00:04:42,534
because you chose this timing when you know that we are preparing to meet the enemy

29
00:04:42,559 --> 00:04:44,415
and the enemy is preparing to meet us.

30
00:04:45,550 --> 00:04:51,926
Nevertheless, that won't prevent me from looking into your concerns.

31
00:04:54,086 --> 00:04:59,197
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) again, his Farasah(فراسه) is never wrong.

32
00:05:01,776 --> 00:05:06,604
He said: I believe that you're lying and you are choosing this time to cause Fitnah(فِتْنَه)

33
00:05:07,617 --> 00:05:13,062
because you know that we are in dire need of having unity now.

34
00:05:13,087 --> 00:05:17,328
So, you know that I'm going to take your concerns very seriously and that's why you chose this timing.

35
00:05:20,566 --> 00:05:26,324
But he said: Nevertheless, I'm not gonna drop this complaint I'm going to look into it.

36
00:05:28,642 --> 00:05:30,632
So, he sent Muhammad Ibn Maslimma(محمدإبن مسلمه),

37
00:05:30,854 --> 00:05:34,100
Muhammad Ibn Maslimma(محمدإبن مسلمه), was the Sahabi(صحابي),

38
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:40,788
who was entrusted with the responsibility of investigating in these issues.

39
00:05:41,764 --> 00:05:43,835
Muhammad Bin Maslimma(محمدإبن مسلمه) is one of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار)

40
00:05:44,375 --> 00:05:50,280
 and by the way, he was the head of the special operations team that assassinated Ka'ab Ibn-e-Ashraf(كعب إبن ألأشرف),

41
00:05:50,518 --> 00:05:52,547
under the commands Rasool Allah ﷺ,

42
00:05:52,872 --> 00:05:57,388
he's very famous name in the books of Seerah(سيرة)

43
00:05:58,004 --> 00:06:02,860
and the Hadith(حديث), that talks about this special mission is in Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ).

44
00:06:03,898 --> 00:06:09,490
So, Muhammad Ibn Maslimma(محمدإبن مسلمه) was one of the well known Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

45
00:06:11,949 --> 00:06:14,805
So, Muhammad Ibn Maslimma(محمدإبن مسلمه), he goes to Al-Kufa(ألكوفه).

46
00:06:16,909 --> 00:06:26,984
And At-Tabri(ألطبري) says: He would take Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص), to each Masjid(مسجد)

47
00:06:29,601 --> 00:06:33,457
and they would hold an assembly with the people, open public meeting

48
00:06:34,671 --> 00:06:39,099
and in front of everyone publicly Muhammad Ibn Maslimma(محمدإبن مسلمه) will say,

49
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:42,376
Do you have anything against your Ameer(أمير) Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص).

50
00:06:45,555 --> 00:06:46,611
And At-Tabri(ألطبري) said;

51
00:06:47,767 --> 00:06:56,243
Because in those days private investigations or investigations in secret, were something that they wouldn't do.

52
00:06:56,853 --> 00:07:00,500
All of their investigations were done in public, public inquiry.

53
00:07:02,290 --> 00:07:06,697
It's not like you go and give the Naseeha(نصيحه) in secretly and silently and not herd know,

54
00:07:06,722 --> 00:07:11,535
when it came to the Wulaa(ولآه), doesn't matter if their feelings are going to be hurt

55
00:07:11,801 --> 00:07:12,695
it's done in public.

56
00:07:13,673 --> 00:07:16,702
Everybody comes in Muhammad Ibn Maslimma(محمدإبن مسلمه) is there

57
00:07:16,895 --> 00:07:18,354
Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص) is there.

58
00:07:18,616 --> 00:07:22,358
If they have anything good, they would say,

59
00:07:22,644 --> 00:07:25,415
if they have anything bad they would say it

60
00:07:25,929 --> 00:07:30,620
and Muhammad Ibn Maslimma(محمدإبن مسلمه), is going to report everything back to Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين).

61
00:07:32,843 --> 00:07:33,612
 At-Tabri(ألطبري) say;

62
00:07:33,972 --> 00:07:39,267
وَلَمْ يَكُنْ أَلّعَمَلْ بِسِّرْمِنْ شَائْنِهِمْ يَوْمَ إِذٍ

63
00:07:40,248 --> 00:07:45,814
They wouldn't do these inquiries privately or secretly, it was public.

64
00:07:48,914 --> 00:07:51,369
They went to each Masjid(مسجد) one by one.

65
00:07:52,586 --> 00:07:57,312
No one had anything bad to say about Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص) nothing negative

66
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:05,827
and these men from Bannu Asad(بنوأسد) would stay quiet

67
00:08:05,932 --> 00:08:08,853
because they wouldn't dare to speak against him publicly.

68
00:08:10,589 --> 00:08:12,392
It's a lie and it would be exposed.

69
00:08:15,407 --> 00:08:19,224
Until, they went to the Masjid(مسجد) of Bannu Abs(بنوعبس).

70
00:08:20,869 --> 00:08:22,922
You have different clans in Al-Kufa(ألكوفه).

71
00:08:24,574 --> 00:08:28,761
Muhammad Ibn Maslimma(محمدإبن مسلمه) is saying; In the name of Allah, I asked you.

72
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:34,330
If you have anything negative to say about Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص) to stand up and say it.

73
00:08:38,241 --> 00:08:41,918
So, one man his name is Usama Bin Qatada(أسامه بن قتادة), he stood up and said;

74
00:08:41,950 --> 00:08:46,909
أَللَّهُمَّ إِنْ نَشَدْتَّنَا فَإِنَّه’ لَا يَقْسِمُ بِسَّوِيَّا،

75
00:08:47,905 --> 00:08:49,493
وَلَا يَعْدِلُوْ فِيْ الرَّيْعَه،

76
00:08:49,979 --> 00:08:51,679
وَلَا يَغْضُوْفِيْ السَّرِيْعَهَ

77
00:08:53,010 --> 00:08:55,538
This man Osama Bin Qatadah(أسامه بن قتادة), he stood up and said;

78
00:08:56,677 --> 00:09:01,539
If you are asking us in the name of Allah to speak the truth then, this is the truth.

79
00:09:03,129 --> 00:09:13,963
Saad(سعد) is a man, who abuses our wealth and he is unjust in his ruling

80
00:09:15,578 --> 00:09:19,160
- and he does not join the Armies.

81
00:09:20,876 --> 00:09:22,509
"He's a coward he stays behind".

82
00:09:24,994 --> 00:09:26,630
Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص) Said:

83
00:09:28,635 --> 00:09:31,946
أَللَّهُمَّ إِنْ كَانَ قَالَهَا كَذِبًا،

84
00:09:32,886 --> 00:09:37,302
وَرِيَاعًا، وَسُمْعَةً،فَأَعْمِيْ بَصَرَ،

85
00:09:37,851 --> 00:09:42,343
وَأَكْثِرْعِيَالَ،وَعَرِّضْه’‘ لِمُذِّلَّآتِلْفِتَنْْ

86
00:09:43,554 --> 00:09:50,855
O Allah if he is lying and he is making these statements to boast and to show off.

87
00:09:52,194 --> 00:09:58,669
Then O Allah blind his eyes and fill his house with dependence

88
00:09:59,947 --> 00:10:03,944
and make him face, the misleading Fittan(فتن).

89
00:10:06,839 --> 00:10:12,974
This man just stands up bluntly and makes such a lie against Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص) in his face.

90
00:10:14,566 --> 00:10:16,524
Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص) was so angry

91
00:10:16,549 --> 00:10:21,053
and there's nothing you can respond back to this man it's fabricated lie, it's a lie.

92
00:10:22,461 --> 00:10:26,561
So, he made this Dua(دُعَا) against him, because it's an outright lie, "slander".

93
00:10:30,933 --> 00:10:39,192
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), this man he lost his sight and when he grew old

94
00:10:39,217 --> 00:10:43,808
he had 10 daughters in his house and he had to take care of them.

95
00:10:46,679 --> 00:10:51,579
And he would chase women in the streets, when he was an old man.

96
00:10:52,813 --> 00:10:58,060
An old man with his eyebrows, covering his eyes and he is blind.

97
00:10:59,001 --> 00:11:02,860
He would go around the streets chasing women.

98
00:11:03,550 --> 00:11:08,101
And when they would come and prevent him from doing that and tell him;

99
00:11:09,152 --> 00:11:14,171
You should have Taqwa(تقوى) in Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and stop what you're doing,

100
00:11:14,195 --> 00:11:16,609
look at you, you're an old man. What are you doing?

101
00:11:17,473 --> 00:11:22,880
He would say: I was hit, I was struck by the Dua(دُعَا) of a blessed man,

102
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:27,318
Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص).

103
00:11:30,789 --> 00:11:32,556
With other men from Bannu Asad(بنوسعد).

104
00:11:33,078 --> 00:11:36,881
Saad Bin Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص) made a Dua(دُعَا) against them. And Said;

105
00:11:36,906 --> 00:11:39,340
اَللَّهُمَّ أَرِّضْهُمْ لِجَهْدِالّبَلَى

106
00:11:39,555 --> 00:11:41,251
"O Allah make their lives difficult."

107
00:11:42,555 --> 00:11:45,055
These men were all killed in a violent death.

108
00:11:45,909 --> 00:11:49,039
One of them was tore into pieces by swords.

109
00:11:50,660 --> 00:11:56,185
The other one was stabbed with the butts of the swords,

110
00:11:56,210 --> 00:12:00,694
with the handles of the swords, until he died and on and on.... with the rest.

111
00:12:01,491 --> 00:12:05,222
All of them were received the wrath of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

112
00:12:05,246 --> 00:12:07,201
because of the Dua(دُعَا) of Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص).

113
00:12:09,337 --> 00:12:11,481
To add to their slander

114
00:12:11,521 --> 00:12:14,727
they said that Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص), doesn't know, how to pray

115
00:12:16,386 --> 00:12:20,037
and he is preoccupied with hunting.

116
00:12:21,895 --> 00:12:23,414
Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص), he said;

117
00:12:25,438 --> 00:12:28,934
إِنِّيْ لَاَوَّلْ رَجُلْ أَحْرَقَ دَمًّا مِنْ الَّمُشْرِكِيْنَ

118
00:12:29,571 --> 00:12:35,090
I'm the first man in Islam to spell the blood of a Mushrik(مشرك), the disbeliever

119
00:12:36,118 --> 00:12:41,843
and I'm the only one whom Rasool Allah ﷺ, sacrificed his father and mother for both.

120
00:12:42,549 --> 00:12:45,721
In Ghazwa of Uhud(غزوةأحَد), Rasool Allah ﷺ would say;

121
00:12:45,746 --> 00:12:48,189
إِرْمِيْ سَعْد فِدَاكَ أَبِيْ وَأُمِّيْ

122
00:12:48,701 --> 00:12:55,606
 O Saad(سعد) shoot them, may my mother and father be sacrifice for you.

123
00:12:57,623 --> 00:13:02,213
Rasool Allah ﷺ was telling Sa'ad(سعد) may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.

124
00:13:02,508 --> 00:13:03,746
Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص) said;

125
00:13:03,875 --> 00:13:09,536
Never did Rasool Allah ﷺ combined both his father and mother for anyone but me

126
00:13:11,187 --> 00:13:14,391
and then he said: And there was a time, when I was one fifth of Islam.

127
00:13:15,078 --> 00:13:16,800
He was the fifth man to become Muslim.

128
00:13:19,551 --> 00:13:22,043
And then Bannu Asad(بنوأسد) claim that I cannot pray.

129
00:13:24,057 --> 00:13:27,807
One of the earliest Muslims given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة) and I cannot pray.

130
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:40,217
Something to learn from this, is beware of the Dua(دُعَا) of the oppressed.

131
00:13:41,238 --> 00:13:43,042
Nothing stands between it and Allah.

132
00:13:44,245 --> 00:13:53,197
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: Allah responds to the prayers of the oppressed even if he is a nonbeliever.

133
00:13:55,154 --> 00:14:00,943
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says: Nothing stands between the Dua(دُعَا) of the oppressed and Allah.

134
00:14:01,766 --> 00:14:04,922
It climbs through the heavens like a spark of lightning.

135
00:14:06,882 --> 00:14:09,566
Nothing stands between it and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

136
00:14:14,216 --> 00:14:17,692
Also you want to be especially careful,

137
00:14:18,375 --> 00:14:27,595
that none of the Aoulea(أوليآء) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, the righteous make a Dua(دُعَا) against you,

138
00:14:30,278 --> 00:14:33,108
 nor should we slander the Aoulea(أوليآء) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

139
00:14:34,932 --> 00:14:39,610
be careful, beware of speaking against the Friends of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

140
00:14:41,083 --> 00:14:47,573
Sometimes that is done to appease the Kuffar(كفار) or it is done because of jealousy

141
00:14:48,249 --> 00:14:55,552
or it's done because we don't agree with their method of work but be very careful.

142
00:14:56,499 --> 00:14:59,363
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ loves some of His servants

143
00:14:59,978 --> 00:15:02,966
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ does not allow anyone to put them down.

144
00:15:05,455 --> 00:15:08,572
So, be careful in the way you use your tongue.

145
00:15:09,808 --> 00:15:15,027
Rasool Allah ﷺ  said: People are thrown in Hellfire on their faces

146
00:15:15,418 --> 00:15:16,880
because of what their tongues reap.

147
00:15:18,207 --> 00:15:23,454
It might be one of the smallest muscles in the body but it's the most dangerous.

148
00:15:24,186 --> 00:15:28,412
Abu Bakr Siddiqueرضي الله عنه would hold his tongue and pull it out and say;

149
00:15:28,693 --> 00:15:30,201
This is, what is getting me in trouble.

150
00:15:32,704 --> 00:15:42,406
They used to say that no one deserves, a long imprisonment term, than your tongue.

151
00:15:45,417 --> 00:15:52,983
Arrest it, and put it in jail and leave it there, give it a life sentence.

152
00:15:55,998 --> 00:16:01,310
Because a word when it comes out of your mouth, it can never be retrieved again.

153
00:16:01,349 --> 00:16:05,858
That's it! It goes out it cannot go back again.

154
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:07,668
If it said it's a done deal.

155
00:16:09,469 --> 00:16:13,418
So, we need to make sure that we use our tongue wisely.

156
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:19,069
These men lost their lives because of slandering Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن ابي وقاص).

157
00:16:20,190 --> 00:16:22,948
Osama Bin Qatada(أسامه بن قتادة), it took him a few seconds

158
00:16:22,979 --> 00:16:26,503
to make that statement in the Masjid(مسجد), he lost his entire life

159
00:16:27,908 --> 00:16:32,876
towards the end of his life an old man running down the street, he is saying;

160
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:34,642
أَصَابَتْنِيْ دَعْوَةٌ الرَّجُلٌ المُبَارَكْ

161
00:16:35,544 --> 00:16:37,828
I was struck by the Dua(دُعَا) of a blessed man.

162
00:16:42,713 --> 00:16:46,503
So, if you ever slandered a righteous man or woman.

163
00:16:47,596 --> 00:16:51,613
If you ever spoke against any of the Aoulea(أوليآء) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

164
00:16:51,894 --> 00:16:53,500
make sure that you make Istaghfar(إستغفار).

165
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:58,214
And make sure that you compensate for talking against them,

166
00:16:58,535 --> 00:17:01,952
by talking for them, by praising them.

167
00:17:03,260 --> 00:17:09,760
The way you do that if you spoke against the person in a meeting of 20 people,

168
00:17:10,428 --> 00:17:16,767
try to find a similar meeting of 20 people and speak good about such a person.

169
00:17:17,933 --> 00:17:20,871
Try to make up for the sin by a similar good deed.

170
00:17:21,519 --> 00:17:23,440
إِنَّ الْحَسَانَاتْ يُذْهِبْنَى السَّيِّئَاتْ

171
00:17:23,878 --> 00:17:26,379
Hasanaat(حسانات) wipe out the sayyiaat(سَيِّئَات),

172
00:17:26,572 --> 00:17:29,172
the good deeds would wipe out the evil ones.

173
00:17:43,836 --> 00:17:54,397
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه received a complaint from one of the soldiers in Egypt.

174
00:17:57,635 --> 00:17:59,647
He told Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه that

175
00:17:59,671 --> 00:18:02,076
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) accused him of being a Munafiq(منافق).

176
00:18:05,963 --> 00:18:09,653
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه summoneds Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

177
00:18:10,967 --> 00:18:12,729
 Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) comes in.

178
00:18:14,292 --> 00:18:18,945
It is established in the court of justice of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

179
00:18:19,323 --> 00:18:23,602
That Amr(عمرو) in fact, did accuse this Muslim soldier of being Munafiq(منافق).

180
00:18:24,583 --> 00:18:30,344
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) gave the soldier a stick

181
00:18:31,395 --> 00:18:40,769
and he told him to discipline Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) for what he has said, against you.

182
00:18:43,898 --> 00:18:45,999
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) is sitting down.

183
00:18:47,649 --> 00:18:51,441
So, the soldier, now this is one of Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص)'s soldiers.

184
00:18:53,025 --> 00:19:02,330
Very low rank and he's now holding the stick ready to hit his leader.

185
00:19:03,595 --> 00:19:08,875
So, he asks, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) he said: Can anyone protect you from me now?

186
00:19:11,410 --> 00:19:14,685
He said: No, go ahead and do what you're commanded to do.

187
00:19:16,944 --> 00:19:23,318
The man said: I forgive you, for the sake of Allah, I forgive you for the sake of Allah.

188
00:19:26,099 --> 00:19:26,828
And he let him go.

189
00:19:30,961 --> 00:19:33,403
So, the honor of people in Islam is protected.

190
00:19:33,791 --> 00:19:35,506
Islam protects five things.

191
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:37,347
Your Deen(دين),

192
00:19:38,699 --> 00:19:39,550
Your life,

193
00:19:41,073 --> 00:19:43,103
Your mind and intellect,

194
00:19:45,073 --> 00:19:45,980
Your wealth

195
00:19:47,002 --> 00:19:48,731
and Your Irz(عِرْضَ) your honor.

196
00:19:49,213 --> 00:19:51,827
These are the five things that Shariah(شريعة) protects.

197
00:19:53,753 --> 00:19:57,928
And there's a special Hadd(حدّ), called Hadd-el- Qadh( حد القض ).

198
00:19:58,676 --> 00:20:00,179
The Hadd(حدّ) of slandering

199
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:11,021
and this is specific for punishing anyone who accuses a righteous Muslim women, of committing Zina(زنا).

200
00:20:12,379 --> 00:20:19,641
However, it would also apply to a man who was accused with the same sin

201
00:20:20,496 --> 00:20:26,124
and also, you would find similar punishment although, it might not exactly be the Qadh(قض) .

202
00:20:26,715 --> 00:20:29,726
It would be a lesser form of punishment.

203
00:20:30,227 --> 00:20:36,802
If a person is dishonored or if somebody was slandered,

204
00:20:37,822 --> 00:20:42,039
 also in such situation a person would be punished.

205
00:20:43,114 --> 00:20:46,712
So, Islam takes the honor of a person very seriously and it's protected

206
00:20:47,466 --> 00:20:54,017
and this soldier, he received justice from Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه

207
00:20:54,325 --> 00:20:59,615
even though it was relating to his own leader, Amr bin Aas رضي الله عنه.

208
00:21:02,781 --> 00:21:03,752
Abu Musa Al Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري)

209
00:21:03,792 --> 00:21:09,169
and we find that all of these Wulaa(ولآه) are great Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

210
00:21:10,611 --> 00:21:12,244
But people can make mistakes

211
00:21:13,041 --> 00:21:16,173
and it also shows that no one was above the law.

212
00:21:17,408 --> 00:21:19,758
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would treat everyone equally,

213
00:21:20,934 --> 00:21:25,215
he could have found justification to say that the Sahabah(صحابه) are above the law

214
00:21:25,449 --> 00:21:27,836
and they should be treated different than everybody else.

215
00:21:28,074 --> 00:21:32,262
Because you people, you became Muslim through them and you owe it to them.

216
00:21:32,782 --> 00:21:39,461
Therefore, they should not be treated equally as you, you owe it to them.

217
00:21:40,358 --> 00:21:43,295
It is a favor that they have done to you.

218
00:21:43,737 --> 00:21:48,872
They have sacrificed their lives and their wealth for your sake, to bring religion to you.

219
00:21:49,636 --> 00:21:51,297
But that's not what Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did.

220
00:21:52,297 --> 00:21:56,512
A new Muslim who just became Muslim can come in

221
00:21:56,969 --> 00:22:00,450
and seek justice against a Sahabi(صحابي) who was a Muslim from day one.

222
00:22:01,329 --> 00:22:07,313
Not only that a non Muslim can come in and go to court like we talked about the case

223
00:22:07,548 --> 00:22:11,428
when a JEW was sitting in court with Ali Ibn Talib رضي الله عنه

224
00:22:12,008 --> 00:22:16,279
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he ruled for the JEW against Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

225
00:22:20,517 --> 00:22:25,473
Abdullah Ibn Umar  رضي الله عنه, he said;

226
00:22:26,536 --> 00:22:33,474
We were accompanying my father, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) we were riding our camels.

227
00:22:35,227 --> 00:22:40,123
When my father spotted someone who was running towards us.

228
00:22:41,517 --> 00:22:47,531
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه said: This is someone who wants to talk to us.

229
00:22:48,543 --> 00:22:49,893
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) stopped.

230
00:22:50,727 --> 00:22:56,250
And this man came and as soon as he saw Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه, he started crying,

231
00:23:00,430 --> 00:23:03,259
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him, what's the matter?

232
00:23:04,458 --> 00:23:05,441
The Man said;

233
00:23:07,531 --> 00:23:15,073
I drank alcohol and your Waali(وآلي), Abu Musa Al Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) flogged me.

234
00:23:16,537 --> 00:23:24,031
But then he humiliated me, by driving me around town exposing me to everyone.

235
00:23:25,465 --> 00:23:29,906
And he told everyone not to eat with me, not to sit with me, not to talk to me.

236
00:23:30,551 --> 00:23:34,930
So, everyone boycotted me, and I was so depressed,

237
00:23:35,856 --> 00:23:39,382
I was thinking about assassinating Abu Musa Al Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري)

238
00:23:41,202 --> 00:23:45,689
or coming to you and asking you to relocate me to another town

239
00:23:46,405 --> 00:23:48,032
where I wouldn't be known.

240
00:23:48,719 --> 00:23:54,664
Or I was thinking about going away from the land of a Islam to land of Kuffr(كفر).

241
00:23:57,173 --> 00:24:00,165
When Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه heard that he started crying.

242
00:24:02,271 --> 00:24:09,974
He said, I would rather sacrifice this, and this, then have you go to the land of disbelief.

243
00:24:11,529 --> 00:24:15,236
And then he wrote a letter to Abu Musa Al Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) and he said;

244
00:24:16,975 --> 00:24:22,525
If you have drove him around the people to expose him and humiliate him,

245
00:24:25,227 --> 00:24:31,084
and you have punished him in public, than I want you to sit down in public and be punished.

246
00:24:32,323 --> 00:24:36,941
and if you did that in private, than I would want you to be punished in private.

247
00:24:39,300 --> 00:24:40,942
And then he told Abu Musa Al Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري)

248
00:24:42,016 --> 00:24:44,748
and if you want to know how serious I am about that,

249
00:24:45,844 --> 00:24:49,586
try doing what you've done again, and you would see what my response would be.

250
00:24:51,807 --> 00:24:58,814
He then gave this man some clothes and 200 Dirham and he told him to go back.

251
00:25:03,892 --> 00:25:14,255
So, brothers and sisters, Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه, he was strict in his rule.

252
00:25:15,763 --> 00:25:19,816
But he had so much mercy in his heart towards the sinners.

253
00:25:21,241 --> 00:25:22,946
This man he drank alcohol.

254
00:25:25,096 --> 00:25:27,620
 He should have been flogged and that was it.

255
00:25:28,850 --> 00:25:34,429
Abu Musa Al Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) carried the punishment further and drove him around exposing him

256
00:25:35,159 --> 00:25:39,402
 and humiliating him in front of everyone, asking the people to boycott him.

257
00:25:40,454 --> 00:25:45,955
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not want the punishment to go beyond the punishment of Sharia(شريعة)

258
00:25:46,836 --> 00:25:49,518
 and Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه told the man

259
00:25:50,127 --> 00:25:54,013
if you drank alcohol, people in the time of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة) used to drink it.

260
00:25:55,692 --> 00:26:00,560
You're not the only person to drink alcohol people in Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة) used to drink it,

261
00:26:01,537 --> 00:26:04,461
you've been punished, that's the end of the story.

262
00:26:04,894 --> 00:26:07,313
The punishment should not carry further than that.

263
00:26:08,475 --> 00:26:15,519
So, when a person commits a sin the punishment is Sharia(شريعة) should be implemented and that's it.

264
00:26:16,685 --> 00:26:21,537
When a man in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ committed adultery,

265
00:26:24,247 --> 00:26:26,206
he was stoned to death.

266
00:26:29,370 --> 00:26:32,904
After they stoned him and he was dead.

267
00:26:34,940 --> 00:26:36,799
Some of the Sahabah(صحابه) said;

268
00:26:38,712 --> 00:26:44,307
This man could not stay quiet and conceal his sin

269
00:26:45,311 --> 00:26:48,707
and he went and talked about it, until he was stoned like a dog.

270
00:26:51,585 --> 00:26:54,310
Rasool Allah ﷺ heard that comment and stayed quiet.

271
00:26:57,522 --> 00:27:08,571
But then he came across a dead animal, decomposed body, foul smell, stench

272
00:27:10,769 --> 00:27:12,734
and he ﷺ told these men to go and eat from it.

273
00:27:14,215 --> 00:27:17,039
They said: O Rasool Ullah can this be eaten.

274
00:27:17,785 --> 00:27:18,729
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

275
00:27:18,769 --> 00:27:24,265
What you have said about your brother earlier is worse than eating from this dead body.

276
00:27:25,402 --> 00:27:31,596
In the name of Allah, the man that you talked about has made a Toba(توبة),

277
00:27:32,454 --> 00:27:36,619
 if it was distributed on the people of Madina, it would be sufficient for them.

278
00:27:38,131 --> 00:27:41,348
And he's now swimming in the rivers of paradise.

279
00:27:43,446 --> 00:27:45,809
He has made a Toba(توبة) he was punished

280
00:27:47,227 --> 00:27:50,340
and now he is in Jannah(جنة) and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ forgave him

281
00:27:51,384 --> 00:27:52,708
just because he committed adultery,

282
00:27:53,081 --> 00:27:58,605
it does not give you a free allowance to say whatever you want against that person,

283
00:27:58,904 --> 00:28:01,261
 he was punished in Shariah(شرية), that was it.!

284
00:28:12,638 --> 00:28:22,711
Another man, he was a man with very loud voice.

285
00:28:23,354 --> 00:28:26,254
So, his voice was helpful in war.

286
00:28:30,461 --> 00:28:32,924
Because of his loud voice, he could rally the army.

287
00:28:34,110 --> 00:28:36,710
And he was also very good in fighting.

288
00:28:41,675 --> 00:28:49,365
He came to Abu Musa(أبوموسى) to claim his portion of the Ghanimah(غنيمه), the spoils of war, the booty.

289
00:28:50,579 --> 00:28:51,928
 Abu Musa(أبوموسى) gave him part of it.

290
00:28:52,109 --> 00:28:53,025
He didn't give him the whole thing.

291
00:28:53,471 --> 00:28:56,416
The man said: I don't want it, either give me all of it or nothing.

292
00:28:57,729 --> 00:29:01,489
Abu Musa(أبوموسى) was angry by the way the man handled this.

293
00:29:01,814 --> 00:29:04,381
So, he flogged him.

294
00:29:09,943 --> 00:29:12,367
So, this man went to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

295
00:29:12,442 --> 00:29:14,348
and also Abu Musa(أبوموسى) shaved his head.

296
00:29:14,957 --> 00:29:17,465
So, the man gathered collected all of his hair.

297
00:29:18,411 --> 00:29:26,774
By the way, shaving the head was a punishment in those days, it was a sign of humiliation.

298
00:29:28,876 --> 00:29:35,037
Shaving the head was a sign of humiliation, it's not stylish.

299
00:29:37,043 --> 00:29:41,978
People only used to shave their heads in Hajj(حَجْ) or Umrah(عمرة) or if they were punished.

300
00:29:44,332 --> 00:29:49,185
It was not Sunnah(سنة) to shave their head in those days.

301
00:29:51,204 --> 00:29:56,003
 So, this man his head was shaved as a punishment,

302
00:29:58,024 --> 00:30:00,363
he collected this hair and he went to Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين)

303
00:30:01,415 --> 00:30:03,789
and he came in to see Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

304
00:30:04,211 --> 00:30:10,039
and he threw the hair on the chest of Umar رضي الله عنه and he said;

305
00:30:10,064 --> 00:30:12,717
If it wasn't for Allah and Hellfire.

306
00:30:13,416 --> 00:30:17,780
Meaning if, it wasn't for Allah and my fear of Hellfire, I would have done so and so.

307
00:30:18,760 --> 00:30:20,817
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him, what happened?

308
00:30:21,721 --> 00:30:25,829
So, the man said: I came to claim my share of the booty.

309
00:30:26,802 --> 00:30:29,165
Abu Musa Al Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) refused to give it to me

310
00:30:29,731 --> 00:30:32,899
and then when I argued with him, he lashed me.

311
00:30:36,382 --> 00:30:43,973
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه had Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري), come to him,

312
00:30:45,395 --> 00:30:52,181
and he gave the whip to this man and told him, take revenge for what he has done against you.

313
00:30:53,299 --> 00:30:59,599
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), these were not men of hatred and evil hearts

314
00:31:00,097 --> 00:31:01,366
they just wanted justice.

315
00:31:02,761 --> 00:31:06,617
So, when he received justice when it was it his hands.

316
00:31:07,301 --> 00:31:10,369
He told Abu Musa Al Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) go! I have forgiven you for the sake of Allah.

317
00:31:11,173 --> 00:31:14,137
Same thing that happened with Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) happens here again.

318
00:31:15,643 --> 00:31:17,605
But they wanted to make a point.

319
00:31:19,751 --> 00:31:27,243
They wanted to prove that we are going to get justice

320
00:31:27,327 --> 00:31:30,319
and we are going to forgive when we have the capability of forgiving.

321
00:31:31,092 --> 00:31:33,934
So, it makes a difference when you forgive and you're able to forgive.

322
00:31:34,462 --> 00:31:38,063
And when you think that you're forgiving when really you only forgiving

323
00:31:38,088 --> 00:31:39,502
because there's nothing else you could do.

324
00:31:40,418 --> 00:31:42,240
There's a difference between both situations.

325
00:31:43,110 --> 00:31:46,978
You get the Ajar(أجر) of forgiving when you are in a position of strength

326
00:31:47,357 --> 00:31:49,950
and you are able to take revenge and then you forgive

327
00:31:50,154 --> 00:31:52,205
that is the forgiveness in which you are rewarded

328
00:31:53,248 --> 00:31:55,076
but when you're the underdog, the weaker one

329
00:31:55,315 --> 00:31:57,990
and then you say, no I forgave him for the sake of Allah

330
00:31:58,015 --> 00:32:01,811
and trying to claim credit for it, to justify your weakness that's something else.

331
00:32:03,518 --> 00:32:05,729
So, over here he had a whip in his hand and

332
00:32:05,754 --> 00:32:08,053
he could have disciplined Abu Musa Al Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري),

333
00:32:08,077 --> 00:32:10,734
but he told him: I forgive you for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

334
00:32:11,020 --> 00:32:11,972
 Go you are free!

335
00:32:19,813 --> 00:32:23,392
Saeed Ibn Aamir(سعيدإبن عامر), one of the Zuhaad(زهاد) of the Sahabah(صحابه),

336
00:32:24,753 --> 00:32:27,643
he was appointed over HIMS(حمص) in Syria.

337
00:32:29,229 --> 00:32:38,012
When Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه met with the delegation of Syria, or the people of Syria from HIMS

338
00:32:38,750 --> 00:32:40,857
 he asked them about Saeed Ibn Aamir(سعيدإبن عامر),

339
00:32:41,844 --> 00:32:42,712
How is he?

340
00:32:43,733 --> 00:32:47,520
They said: We have no complaints against him except for four things.

341
00:32:49,338 --> 00:32:50,409
Number 1)

342
00:32:52,472 --> 00:32:54,358
He shows up to work late.

343
00:32:57,862 --> 00:32:58,866
Number 2)

344
00:32:59,858 --> 00:33:01,445
We would never see him at night,

345
00:33:01,660 --> 00:33:08,424
we might have an emergency need, we would knock on his door

346
00:33:08,600 --> 00:33:12,079
they didn't really have doors in those days, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) we'll talk about that.

347
00:33:12,112 --> 00:33:15,291
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) banned his governors from having doors.

348
00:33:16,555 --> 00:33:19,540
So, they will come and call them actually, from their name.

349
00:33:22,983 --> 00:33:24,883
He would never come out at night.

350
00:33:25,254 --> 00:33:26,206
Number 3)

351
00:33:26,730 --> 00:33:30,672
One day per week, he would disappear, we have no idea where he goes.

352
00:33:31,777 --> 00:33:32,624
Number 4)

353
00:33:32,926 --> 00:33:38,124
Sometimes he would be sitting in court and he would just fall unconscious,

354
00:33:40,301 --> 00:33:41,275
he would just drop.

355
00:33:44,066 --> 00:33:46,034
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was worried

356
00:33:47,201 --> 00:33:55,545
because his Farasah(فراسہ), his intuition about Saeed Ibn Aamir(سعيدإبن عامر), was that he was one of the best.

357
00:33:56,651 --> 00:34:01,439
So, he was very concerned when he heard these accusations.

358
00:34:02,134 --> 00:34:07,603
In fact, he said when he heard the first one, he shows up late to work,

359
00:34:07,997 --> 00:34:08,933
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

360
00:34:08,997 --> 00:34:09,834
 "إِنَّهَاالّعَظِيْمَهْ"

361
00:34:09,858 --> 00:34:13,151
This is a great fatal mistake.

362
00:34:15,159 --> 00:34:17,024
How come he's going to work late.?

363
00:34:18,732 --> 00:34:26,362
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him; to come and to face his accusers in court.

364
00:34:27,646 --> 00:34:30,953
So, he asked them first what complaints do you have?

365
00:34:30,978 --> 00:34:34,003
They said: Number one, he shows up late to work.

366
00:34:34,578 --> 00:34:35,373
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said:

