566
00:51:42,434 --> 00:51:45,214
could cover the naked bodies of many Muslims

567
00:51:45,239 --> 00:51:47,496
and save them from hot weather and cold weather.

568
00:51:53,485 --> 00:52:00,796
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would go as far as disciplining them physically with his famous stick Ad-Durra(ألدّره),

569
00:52:01,986 --> 00:52:04,390
 he did that a couple of times

570
00:52:05,498 --> 00:52:09,461
not only did he use a durra(درَّة) but once when he went to Ash-Sham(ألشام),

571
00:52:11,194 --> 00:52:15,367
Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة), Yazeed Ibn Abi Sufiaan(يزيدإبن أبي سفيان) and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

572
00:52:15,956 --> 00:52:21,690
they came to meet, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه and they had some nice clothes on.

573
00:52:23,221 --> 00:52:27,253
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) saw them he came down from this camel.

574
00:52:27,820 --> 00:52:30,518
Picked up some rocks and started throwing at them,

575
00:52:31,566 --> 00:52:35,769
pelting Yazeed(يزيد), Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) and Khalid(خالد) imagine throwing rocks at them.

576
00:52:38,564 --> 00:52:39,460
And then he said;

577
00:52:40,210 --> 00:52:45,699
مَا أَسْرَأَ مَا رَجَعْتُمْ أَنْ رَّيْكُمْ،إِيَّايَ تَسْتَقْبِلُوْنَ فِيْ هَذَا ذِّي

578
00:52:46,648 --> 00:52:49,438
How fast have you changed your ways?

579
00:52:50,029 --> 00:52:52,696
How dare you meet me with these clothes?

580
00:52:53,390 --> 00:52:55,274
وَإِنَّمَا شَبِئْتُمْ مُنْزُ سَنَتَيْنَ

581
00:52:55,448 --> 00:52:57,476
You only knew wealth two years ago.

582
00:52:58,424 --> 00:53:02,514
وَبِاللهِ وَلَوْ فَعَلْتُمْ هَذَا عَلَى رَئْسِلْ مِئَتَيْنِ لَسْتَبْدِلْ بِكُمْ غَيْرَكُمْ

583
00:53:02,815 --> 00:53:08,053
 In the name of Allah. If you did this after 200 years from now, I wouldn't have accepted it.

584
00:53:08,957 --> 00:53:11,008
He is telling them two years ago, you are poor.

585
00:53:11,580 --> 00:53:15,227
And now you tasted wealth and you already changed within two years.

586
00:53:16,106 --> 00:53:20,232
Even if you are wealthy for 200 years, I wouldn't have allowed this change to show on you.

587
00:53:21,373 --> 00:53:25,959
You're working with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), you're gonna have to carry on with the old ways,

588
00:53:26,880 --> 00:53:28,807
 even if it's going to last for 200 years.

589
00:53:33,589 --> 00:53:38,349
He reduced the status of one of his governors from being a governor, to being a shepherd

590
00:53:40,264 --> 00:53:42,830
Ayaaz Bin Ghanam(أياز بن غنم), he appointed him as a governor.

591
00:53:42,854 --> 00:53:50,129
So, Ayaaz(أياز) he built a new house and he built himself a bath

592
00:53:51,777 --> 00:53:56,646
and he also had a special group

593
00:53:58,820 --> 00:54:03,509
which he would spend his night with and talk with exclusive group.

594
00:54:04,832 --> 00:54:09,248
And this was not accessible for the rest of the people,

595
00:54:09,990 --> 00:54:13,052
 special group that are close to the Ameer(أمير).

596
00:54:13,958 --> 00:54:18,824
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) call him to Madina, he comes in, he brings 300 sheep.

597
00:54:21,495 --> 00:54:30,302
He gives it to him and he gives him a wool rough Thaub(ثوب), he tells him wear this.

598
00:54:32,411 --> 00:54:35,342
And then he tells him: Take these goats or sheep.

599
00:54:36,217 --> 00:54:37,397
So, he would walk away

600
00:54:38,051 --> 00:54:43,692
and when he is far from Umar(عُمَر), Umar(عُمَر) would tell him: Come back, come back.

601
00:54:44,030 --> 00:54:48,165
And he's next to Umar(عُمَر), go away. You go away, come back.

602
00:54:48,817 --> 00:54:55,461
And you would have him go back and forth with the 300 sheep until, he started sweating.

603
00:54:56,806 --> 00:55:01,400
And then he said: Go and take them out to the pasture land and then come back.

604
00:55:01,759 --> 00:55:05,064
He would go out to the pasture land and come back, go and water them

605
00:55:06,337 --> 00:55:08,623
and he would have him go back and forth for two months.

606
00:55:12,161 --> 00:55:16,356
After two months, he told him: Do you still want a bath in your house?

607
00:55:17,583 --> 00:55:19,825
Do you still want to have an exclusive group around you?

608
00:55:20,324 --> 00:55:23,105
He said: No Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), that's it, I don't want that anymore.

609
00:55:23,237 --> 00:55:25,894
Toba(توبة)! I repent to Allah.

610
00:55:27,715 --> 00:55:30,121
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), this disciplining made Ayaaz Bin Ghanam(أياز بن غنم)

611
00:55:30,135 --> 00:55:32,810
one of the best governors of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

612
00:55:36,034 --> 00:55:43,856
He would ask them to split their wealth in half, after they leave their job.

613
00:55:44,431 --> 00:55:46,817
We said earlier that he would take the difference.

614
00:55:47,079 --> 00:55:49,934
Over here it's contradicting narration.

615
00:55:51,485 --> 00:55:54,000
It says that for example, they started,

616
00:55:54,802 --> 00:55:59,115
so he would hold an account for them before they assume the job.

617
00:55:59,155 --> 00:56:01,179
Let's say they had 1000 Dinar(دينار).

618
00:56:01,670 --> 00:56:04,767
After he removes them from the job.

619
00:56:04,807 --> 00:56:07,188
Let's say they had 2000 Dinar(دينار).

620
00:56:08,047 --> 00:56:09,907
So, the difference is a 1000 Dinar(دينار).

621
00:56:09,947 --> 00:56:12,196
They made a 1000 Dinar(دينار) within that period.

622
00:56:12,375 --> 00:56:14,699
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would ask them to split it in half.

623
00:56:16,417 --> 00:56:18,931
Allah Ho Alam(ألله أعلم) which narration is stronger.

624
00:56:20,082 --> 00:56:21,844
But I'm mentioning to you both.

625
00:56:25,260 --> 00:56:27,426
That's what he did with Khalid Ibn Waleed رضي الله عنه.

626
00:56:28,572 --> 00:56:32,484
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said: He split everything in half, even my shoes.

627
00:56:33,622 --> 00:56:36,862
He would take one pair, he would take one and we give me one.

628
00:56:41,968 --> 00:56:49,402
He would reprimand them verbally and he would write letters to them.

629
00:56:51,910 --> 00:56:55,274
When he went to meet with Muawiya Bin Abi Sufiyan(معاويه بن أبي سفيان).

630
00:56:57,513 --> 00:56:59,952
Muawiya(معاويه) came to meet him in an entourage.

631
00:57:01,661 --> 00:57:05,557
Muawiya(معاويه) is the new governor in Syria and he comes to meet

632
00:57:06,550 --> 00:57:09,628
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه and he is surrounded by guards.

633
00:57:13,339 --> 00:57:16,003
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was riding his camel.

634
00:57:16,767 --> 00:57:23,913
Muawiya(معاويه) came down out of respect to greet the Khalifah(خليفه).

635
00:57:25,810 --> 00:57:30,315
The Khalifah(خليفه) ignores him and he is walking away on his camel

636
00:57:31,266 --> 00:57:36,622
and Muawiya(معاويه) is now running on foot after the Khalifah(خليفه),

637
00:57:37,406 --> 00:57:42,027
trying to get his attention, and Muawiya(معاويه) was a heavy man.

638
00:57:43,323 --> 00:57:45,506
So, he was catching his breath, he was gasping

639
00:57:46,744 --> 00:57:49,412
and Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه is ignoring him.

640
00:57:50,448 --> 00:57:54,106
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) felt pity for Muawiya(معاويه).

641
00:57:54,131 --> 00:57:55,441
He said: O Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين),

642
00:57:55,474 --> 00:57:56,354
 "أَتَعَبْتَ الرَّجُلْ"

643
00:57:56,449 --> 00:57:57,309
 He is exhausted.

644
00:57:58,225 --> 00:57:59,356
Please talk to him.

645
00:58:00,682 --> 00:58:02,834
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) turns around and said;

646
00:58:04,929 --> 00:58:06,365
Who does this entourage belong to?

647
00:58:07,984 --> 00:58:09,048
He said: It belongs to me.

648
00:58:10,204 --> 00:58:18,664
He said: It belongs to you and in addition to that, I hear that you have an officer

649
00:58:19,863 --> 00:58:21,711
who stands between you and men.

650
00:58:22,227 --> 00:58:23,473
 When people want to meet you?

651
00:58:23,832 --> 00:58:27,528
You had a secretary, now Muawiya(معاويه) had a secretary,

652
00:58:27,568 --> 00:58:30,717
if you want to meet Muawiya(معاويه) you have to come through his secretary.

653
00:58:33,709 --> 00:58:34,960
Muawiya(معاويه) said: Yes.

654
00:58:36,151 --> 00:58:37,785
He said: Woe to you. Why did you do that?

655
00:58:38,733 --> 00:58:44,114
Muawiya(معاويه) said: O Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) in this land of ours,

656
00:58:44,696 --> 00:58:50,419
there are plenty of spies planted by our enemy.

657
00:58:52,657 --> 00:58:56,535
If they see us moving around without heavy security.

658
00:58:58,251 --> 00:59:01,306
They might take advantage of that and attack us

659
00:59:03,767 --> 00:59:05,877
and the reason, why I have a secretary

660
00:59:06,907 --> 00:59:11,616
is because I don't want the people to take advantage of us.

661
00:59:13,509 --> 00:59:15,988
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه said: O Muawiya(معاويه),

662
00:59:17,058 --> 00:59:20,312
whenever, I ask you about something you have a justification for it.

663
00:59:22,263 --> 00:59:24,186
If what you're saying is true.

664
00:59:24,614 --> 00:59:26,773
That is very intelligent of you

665
00:59:27,255 --> 00:59:32,735
and if what you're saying is a lie, that's a very clever lie.

666
00:59:36,023 --> 00:59:40,163
 I do not approve or disapprove what you're doing.

667
00:59:40,425 --> 00:59:41,323
He left it at that.

668
00:59:42,421 --> 00:59:46,058
because Muawiya(معاويه) told him after he mentioned his justification is he said;

669
00:59:46,386 --> 00:59:51,012
And after that I am only your servant.

670
00:59:51,687 --> 00:59:53,734
If you tell me to go on with it, I would,

671
00:59:53,816 --> 00:59:55,527
- if you tell me to stop, I would.

672
00:59:57,265 --> 01:00:00,182
So, Umar(عُمَر) said: You know how to get out of trouble.

673
01:00:10,613 --> 01:00:11,613
Tayeb(طيب)

674
01:00:15,608 --> 01:00:17,719
In Sha Allah Ho Ta'ala(إن شاء الله تعالى) tomorrow night,

675
01:00:18,045 --> 01:00:24,856
we will either move on to the section on the Ghazawaat(غزوات) , the battles,

676
01:00:26,178 --> 01:00:33,911
or we will jump ahead and talk about the death of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

677
01:00:33,936 --> 01:00:36,201
and then talk about the battles, after that.

678
01:00:38,868 --> 01:00:43,655
So, we're done with the section relating to the Wulaa(وُلأء) of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

679
01:00:43,813 --> 01:00:48,025
IT SHUDDERS IN PAIN FREELY

680
01:00:48,242 --> 01:00:52,384
MY CHASITY, MY MODESTY!

681
01:00:52,500 --> 01:00:56,721
OH MUSLIM, YOU SAW

682
01:00:56,855 --> 01:01:01,155
MY INJURY AND THE INJURY OF MY PRIDE

